{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"350","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Bombs"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You've got a robot, its task is destroying bombs on a square plane. Specifically, the square plane contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" bombs, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bomb is at point with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(xi, yi)"},{"kind":"text","text":". We know that no two bombs are at the same point and that no bomb is at point with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Initially, the robot is at point with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also, let's mark the robot's current position as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":". In order to destroy all the bombs, the robot can perform three types of operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Operation has format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 k dir"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". To perform the operation robot have to move in direction "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"dir"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k ≥ 1"},{"kind":"text","text":") times. There are only "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" directions the robot can move in: \"R\", \"L\", \"U\", \"D\". During one move the robot can move from the current point to one of following points: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x + 1, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x - 1, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" (corresponding to directions). It is forbidden to move from point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", if at least one point on the path (besides the destination point) contains a bomb. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Operation has format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". To perform the operation robot have to pick a bomb at point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and put it in a special container. Thus, the robot can carry the bomb from any point to any other point. The operation cannot be performed if point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":" has no bomb. It is forbidden to pick a bomb if the robot already has a bomb in its container. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Operation has format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". To perform the operation robot have to take a bomb out of the container and destroy it. You are allowed to perform this operation only if the robot is at point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is forbidden to perform the operation if the container has no bomb. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the robot and find the shortest possible sequence of operations he can perform to destroy all bombs on the coordinate plane."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of bombs on the coordinate plane. Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain two integers each. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(xi, yi)"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ xi, yi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the coordinates of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bomb. It is guaranteed that no two bombs are located at the same point and no bomb is at point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the minimum number of operations needed to destroy all bombs. On the next lines print the descriptions of these "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" operations. If there are multiple sequences, you can print any of them. It is guaranteed that there is the solution where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1 1\n-1 -1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n1 1 R\n1 1 U\n2\n1 1 L\n1 1 D\n3\n1 1 L\n1 1 D\n2\n1 1 R\n1 1 U\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n5 0\n0 5\n1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n1 1 R\n2\n1 1 L\n3\n1 5 R\n2\n1 5 L\n3\n1 5 U\n2\n1 5 D\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"350C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/350/problem/C"}